WEBVTT

00:00.290 --> 00:02.280
- [Instructor] We're told
that Lauren uses a blend

00:02.280 --> 00:04.610
of dark roast beans and light roast beans

00:04.610 --> 00:06.780
to make coffee at her cafe.

00:06.780 --> 00:11.580
She needs 80 kilograms of beans
in total for her next order.

00:11.580 --> 00:14.750
Dark roast beans cost $3 per kilogram,

00:14.750 --> 00:17.770
light roast beans cost $2 per kilogram,

00:17.770 --> 00:20.920
and she wants to spend $220 in total.

00:20.920 --> 00:22.960
And they tell us here's a graph

00:22.960 --> 00:26.060
that shows a system of
equations for this scenario

00:26.060 --> 00:28.680
where x is the number of kilograms

00:28.680 --> 00:30.790
of dark roast beans she buys

00:30.790 --> 00:33.390
and y is the number of kilograms

00:33.390 --> 00:35.880
of light roast beans she buys.

00:35.880 --> 00:39.180
All right, let me scroll down
so we can take a look at this.

00:39.180 --> 00:42.930
And so sure enough, so this blue line,

00:42.930 --> 00:44.900
and I'll write it out in blue,

00:44.900 --> 00:48.090
this x is the number of
kilograms of dark roast beans,

00:48.090 --> 00:51.170
y is the number of kilograms
of light roast beans,

00:51.170 --> 00:53.930
and she wants to buy a
total of 80 kilograms.

00:53.930 --> 00:56.300
That's what they told us up here.

00:56.300 --> 00:58.640
We can go back to look at that.

00:58.640 --> 01:01.340
She needs, I'll underline this in blue.

01:01.340 --> 01:05.000
She needs 80 kilograms of beans.

01:05.000 --> 01:08.050
So that constraint that
the sum of the kilograms

01:08.050 --> 01:10.490
of dark and light is equal to 80,

01:10.490 --> 01:12.270
that's represented by this equation.

01:12.270 --> 01:13.710
And if we were to graph it,

01:13.710 --> 01:16.610
that is this blue line right over here.

01:16.610 --> 01:20.350
And then this other constraint, three x,

01:20.350 --> 01:23.030
well, the dark roast beans
cost $3 per kilogram,

01:23.030 --> 01:25.730
so three x is how much
she spends on dark roast.

01:25.730 --> 01:27.920
Two y is how much she
spends on light roast

01:27.920 --> 01:30.190
'cause it's $2 per kilogram.

01:30.190 --> 01:32.680
And 220 is the amount
that she spends in total.

01:32.680 --> 01:35.310
And they tell us that up here.

01:35.310 --> 01:38.120
Dark roast beans cost $3 per kilogram,

01:38.120 --> 01:40.740
light roast beans cost $2 per kilogram,

01:40.740 --> 01:43.760
and she wants to spend $220.

01:43.760 --> 01:46.690
So this equation is
another way of expressing

01:46.690 --> 01:49.400
what I just underlined up here in green.

01:49.400 --> 01:53.170
And the green line shows all

01:53.170 --> 01:58.170
of the x y combinations that
would match these constraints.

01:59.130 --> 02:01.890
And so now let's do something interesting.

02:01.890 --> 02:05.510
They've labeled some points
here, point C, D, F, and E.

02:05.510 --> 02:07.020
And we're gonna think about what do each

02:07.020 --> 02:08.190
of these points represent?

02:08.190 --> 02:13.190
So for example, this point
C that is on the green line,

02:13.470 --> 02:17.600
but it sits above the blue line,

02:17.600 --> 02:19.030
what does this tell us?

02:19.030 --> 02:20.630
What does this point C represent?

02:20.630 --> 02:22.430
Pause this video and think about it.

02:24.020 --> 02:26.070
Well, if we're on the green line,

02:26.070 --> 02:29.430
that means that the amount
that she spends on dark roast

02:29.430 --> 02:33.080
plus the amount that she spends
on light roast is adding up

02:33.080 --> 02:35.790
to exactly $220.

02:35.790 --> 02:40.450
So she's definitely spending $220 at C,

02:40.450 --> 02:44.590
but how many total kilograms is she using?

02:44.590 --> 02:48.470
Well, the fact that for this given x,

02:48.470 --> 02:50.880
we're sitting above the line,

02:50.880 --> 02:54.917
that means that she's not
using exactly 80 kilograms.

02:54.917 --> 02:56.530
And we can see that over here.

02:56.530 --> 02:59.620
She's using, looks like
10 kilograms of dark,

02:59.620 --> 03:04.400
and it looks like something
like 95 kilograms of light.

03:04.400 --> 03:06.870
If you were to add those
two points together,

03:06.870 --> 03:10.340
it looks like she's using
something closer to 105 kilograms.

03:10.340 --> 03:11.820
So point C is a situation

03:11.820 --> 03:14.710
where she is spending exactly $220,

03:14.710 --> 03:18.750
but she's using more than 80 kilograms

03:18.750 --> 03:20.830
'cause it's not meeting
this second constraint.

03:20.830 --> 03:22.750
It's sitting above that line.

03:22.750 --> 03:23.750
Now let's think about point D.

03:23.750 --> 03:24.900
What does that represent?

03:24.900 --> 03:27.660
Pause the video and
try to figure that out.

03:27.660 --> 03:30.500
Well, because we sit on the blue line,

03:30.500 --> 03:33.140
that means that we are
meeting this constraint

03:33.140 --> 03:37.500
that the kilograms of
dark and light combined

03:37.500 --> 03:40.000
is equal to 80 kilograms.

03:40.000 --> 03:43.200
So she's using exactly 80 kilograms here,

03:43.200 --> 03:45.450
but what about her spending?

03:45.450 --> 03:49.440
Well, because this point
lies below the green line,

03:49.440 --> 03:52.200
that tells us that we are spending

03:52.200 --> 03:55.017
less than $220.

03:55.017 --> 03:56.730
And we could even try it out.

03:56.730 --> 04:01.730
Three times 20 plus two times 60 is what?

04:01.840 --> 04:05.150
60 plus 120 is $180.

04:05.150 --> 04:08.590
And so this is a point where
we're meeting this constraint,

04:08.590 --> 04:10.070
but we're not meeting this constraint.

04:10.070 --> 04:12.680
We're underspending right over here.

04:12.680 --> 04:14.810
Now, what about point F?

04:14.810 --> 04:18.080
Well, point F sits below
both of these lines.

04:18.080 --> 04:20.683
So pause your video and
think about what that means.

04:21.590 --> 04:24.930
Well, if we're sitting
below both of these lines,

04:24.930 --> 04:29.510
that means that neither
are we spending $220,

04:29.510 --> 04:32.500
nor are we using 80 kilograms.

04:32.500 --> 04:34.620
And you can see that if you
actually look at the numbers.

04:34.620 --> 04:35.610
You don't have to do this,

04:35.610 --> 04:37.860
but this is just to make
you feel good about it.

04:37.860 --> 04:41.020
It looks like she is
using 30 kilograms of dark

04:41.020 --> 04:45.480
and 30 kilograms of light,
so in total she is using,

04:45.480 --> 04:46.670
so this is a situation

04:46.670 --> 04:49.740
where she's using 60
kilograms in total, not 80.

04:49.740 --> 04:52.080
And so that's why we're not
sitting on this blue line.

04:52.080 --> 04:54.070
And if you look at how
much she's spending,

04:54.070 --> 04:55.740
she has 30 kilograms of each,

04:55.740 --> 04:58.140
so three times 30 plus two times 30,

04:58.140 --> 05:00.390
that's going to be 90 plus 60.

05:00.390 --> 05:02.057
That's also less than 220,

05:02.057 --> 05:06.000
and so that's why we see this
point is below these lines.

05:06.000 --> 05:09.283
And then last but not least,
what does point E represent?

05:10.470 --> 05:13.170
Well, point E sits on both of these lines,

05:13.170 --> 05:16.410
so that means that it meets
both of these constraints.

05:16.410 --> 05:20.740
This is a situation where
she is spending exactly $220,

05:20.740 --> 05:23.770
and the total number of
kilograms she's using

05:23.770 --> 05:26.490
of dark and light is exactly 80.

05:26.490 --> 05:29.250
And so if we wanted to
say, hey, what combination

05:29.250 --> 05:31.950
of dark and light would she need

05:31.950 --> 05:35.660
in order to meet both
constraints, E represents that,

05:35.660 --> 05:37.953
the intersection of these two lines.
